  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "0",
      "text": "Callouts"
    },
    {
      "id": "1",
      "text": "Note: This type of callout is an ordinary note or tip."
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "text": "Caution: This type of callout suggests proceeding with caution."
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "text": "Warning: This type of callout is stronger than a Caution; it means \"Don't do this.\""
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "text": "Success: This type of callout describes a successful action or an error-free status. Used only in interactive or dynamic content; don't use in ordinary static pages."
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "text": "Key Point: This type of callout defines an important concept."
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "text": "Key Term: This type of callout defines important terminology."
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "text": "Objective: This type of callout defines the goal of a procedure."
    },
    {
      "id": "8",
      "text": "Dogfood: This type of callout is for notes that apply temporarily during internal dogfood testing. Remove all Dogfood callouts before making a document publicly visible."
    },
    {
      "id": "9",
      "text": "Comparisons"
    },
    {
      "id": "10",
      "text": "Not recommended — indent with tabs"
    },
    {
      "id": "11",
      "text": "{code1}(bad sample code)\n{/code1}"
    },
    {
      "id": "12",
      "text": "Recommended — indent with spaces"
    },
    {
      "id": "13",
      "text": "{code1}(good sample code)\n{/code1}"
    },
    {
      "id": "14",
      "text": "Not allowed — indent with spaces"
    },
    {
      "id": "15",
      "text": "{code1}(very bad sample code)\n{/code1}"
    },
    {
      "id": "16",
      "text": "External links"
    },
    {
      "id": "17",
      "text": "To mark a link as external, use\n{code1}&#x3C;a href=\"https://www.google.com/\" class=\"external\">External Link&#x3C;/a>{/code1} when\nauthoring in HTML, or append {code2}{: .external}{/code2} to links when authoring in\nMarkdown."
    },
    {
      "id": "18",
      "text": "{a1}External Link{/a1}",
      "attributes": {
        "a1": {
          "href": "https://www.google.com/"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "19",
      "text": "Custom attributes and named anchors"
    },
    {
      "id": "20",
      "text": "Markdown supports custom markup attributes for block level HTML elements and\nheaders."
    },
    {
      "id": "21",
      "text": "The format for this allows for a custom class, a custom ID, and/or custom\nattribute/value pairs in the same statement:"
    },
    {
      "id": "22",
      "text": "{code1}This is a paragraph.\n{: .customClass #custom_id attribute='value' }\n{/code1}"
    },
    {
      "id": "23",
      "text": "This generates this HTML:"
    },
    {
      "id": "24",
      "text": "{code1}&#x3C;p class=\"customClass\" id=\"custom_id\" attribute=\"value\">This is a paragraph.&#x3C;/p>\n{/code1}"
    },
    {
      "id": "25",
      "text": "Custom attributes on headers"
    },
    {
      "id": "26",
      "text": "As headers can only be defined in one line, the attributes list should be\ndefined at the end of the header definition:"
    },
    {
      "id": "27",
      "text": "{code1}## Header with custom ID {: #custom_id }\n{/code1}"
    },
    {
      "id": "28",
      "text": "Generates:"
    },
    {
      "id": "29",
      "text": "{code1}&#x3C;h2 id=\"custom_id\">Header with custom ID&#x3C;/h2>\n{/code1}"
    },
    {
      "id": "30",
      "text": "Block quote"
    },
    {
      "id": "31",
      "text": "{code1}> Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit.\n{/code1}"
    },
    {
      "id": "32",
      "text": "Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit."
    },
    {
      "id": "33",
      "text": "Tooltips"
    },
    {
      "id": "34",
      "text": "Any element that has a {code1}title{/code1} attribute will show a tooltip (with the value\nof the attribute) on mouseover. For example: \"...someday screen\nPPI may increase further...\"\n(note that the dotted underline comes from the abbr element, not the tooltip)."
    },
    {
      "id": "35",
      "text": "{code1}...someday screen &#x3C;abbr title=\"pixels per inch\">PPI&#x3C;/abbr> may increase further...\n{/code1}"
    },
    {
      "id": "36",
      "text": "Warning: Be sure to use tooltips only for supplemental information—not essential text or primary user-experience features—since the presence of tooltips is not obvious and users on mobile devices will not see them at all."
    },
    {
      "id": "37",
      "text": "Miscellaneous classes"
    },
    {
      "id": "38",
      "text": "Use {code1}class=\"inline\"{/code1}, {code2}class=\"inline-block\"{/code2}, and {code3}class=\"block\"{/code3} to force\ninline, inline-block, or block layout, in the rare cases when it is necessary."
    },
    {
      "id": "39",
      "text": "Use {code1}class=\"clearfix\"{/code1} to clear a floated element, for example after using\n{code2}attempt-left{/code2} or {code3}attempt-right{/code3}."
    }
  ]
}
